# sentence_id = 82
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = And to care for one's own body in due measure, neither as one overly fond of life nor out of vanity, yet not carelessly either, but so attentive to it that through such personal care one had very little need of medicine, of drugs, or of external applications.
# literal_translation = And [I learned]: the caring-for of [one's] own body, in due measure—neither as if someone were fond-of-life, nor for the sake of adornment, nor yet carelessly—but so as: through [one's] own attentiveness, to have need of very few things of medicine, or of drugs and of poultices, from outside.
